    "designation": {
      "label": "tt-tnt-1024a",
      "hf_model": "/home/ttuser/code/tt-tnt/artifacts/hf-tt-tnt-1024a",
      "reason": "At a MATCHED 512-token window it is the lowest-loss checkpoint this project has: capacity is worth -0.2994 nats on average against the 384s512 control and is negative at 22/22 checkpoints (sign test p ~ 4.8e-7, sd 0.0538), where the seed-only control wanders across sign (8/22 negative, sd 0.1944). Final matched-window validation loss 2.9281 vs 384s512's 3.1938.",
      "qualification": "\"Best\" here is not unqualified. 1024a is trained at a 512 context while v3/v4/v5 are trained at 2048, so 1024a serves a quarter of the context and its loss advantage is only established AT 512 -- the two are not comparable at v3's own window, and this repo has already published one wrong headline by treating a 512-window loss and a 2048-window loss as commensurable. 1024a is also 123.0M parameters against v3's 22M, so it is the slower model to serve. Its register advantage over v3 was substantially CONTEXT, not capacity: the clean capacity leg (384s512 -> 1024a) moves the tinystories margin only 1.03x the seed floor, which is a null by this project's standing rule.",
